(5626112, 816742, 86447, '<td valign="top">A bit over neatened... but still it''s a 7.  Would have been an 8, though.<br/> <br/>ETA:  Looking again at this, I think it''s not really the smoothness, that''s kinda cool in a way... it''s the extra stem being so in focus that detracts.  I know that''s impossible to control, but it does affect the photo.<br/> <br/>The colors are wonderful.</td>', 'A bit over neatened... but still it''s a 7.  Would have been an 8, though. ETA:  Looking again at this, I think it''s not really the smoothness, that''s kinda cool in a way... it''s the extra stem being so in focus that detracts.  I know that''s impossible to control, but it does affect the photo. The colors are wonderful.', '2009-08-27 11:02:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5626183, 816593, 86447, '<td valign="top">Looks like a heavy crop maybe?... so it''s poor image quality, but still charming.<br/> <br/>ETA: Looking at this again in the daylight, I think the image quality problem might be due to the basic''s 150K max.  It''s better viewed in the daylight, but still the jaggies are distracting to me.   I''m staying with my vote of a 6 because it''s clearly a Thirds image and it''s so charming.  <br/> <br/>How''dyagetem to pose for you like that?  *grin*</td>', 'Looks like a heavy crop maybe?... so it''s poor image quality, but still charming. ETA: Looking at this again in the daylight, I think the image quality problem might be due to the basic''s 150K max.  It''s better viewed in the daylight, but still the jaggies are distracting to me.   I''m staying with my vote of a 6 because it''s clearly a Thirds image and it''s so charming.   How''dyagetem to pose for you like that?  *grin*', '2009-08-27 12:24:31.000000', NULL, 1),
