(5634802, 816697, 71537, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the votes and messages. I had another idea for rule of the thirds ... while cycling around the lake of Zug in Switzerland (//www.trailguru.com/wiki/index.php/Track:8Z0M) ... I saw a road sign which was showing forbidden for cars, motorbikes ... it was splited in three and behind was a superb sunset ... I went home grab my camera and wanted to shoot that sign using rule of the thirds and showing the rule of the thirds :) ... but my daughter stopped me on the way ... then I realized I will arive too late there ... so I took a photo of these three girls watching the lake from a bench ... probably would have been more nicer with some basic editig, but I had no time ... maybe next time<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thank you all for the votes and messages. I had another idea for rule of the thirds ... while cycling around the lake of Zug in Switzerland (//www.trailguru.com/wiki/index.php/Track:8Z0M) ... I saw a road sign which was showing forbidden for cars, motorbikes ... it was splited in three and behind was a superb sunset ... I went home grab my camera and wanted to shoot that sign using rule of the thirds and showing the rule of the thirds :) ... but my daughter stopped me on the way ... then I realized I will arive too late there ... so I took a photo of these three girls watching the lake from a bench ... probably would have been more nicer with some basic editig, but I had no time ... maybe next time ', '2009-09-03 18:12:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5634854, 816810, 43774, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your ribbon, totally deserving of the blue. For some reason this reminds me of Japanese art.</td>', 'Congratulations on your ribbon, totally deserving of the blue. For some reason this reminds me of Japanese art.', '2009-09-03 19:01:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5634963, 816182, 59029, '<td valign="top">Background not doing you any favours, but otherwise a compelling subject very good composition.  Crop a little tight on the bottom but otherwise he would''ve run out of head space!  <br/> <br/>Don''t be afraid to play with the camera settings.  If you do as I did, and sometimes still do, shoot on Auto, take a look at what the camera chose and the result you got.  Now, you can go to Manual mode and basically replicate those settings for a baseline, then mess around a little with the aperture and shutter speeds, and see what happens.<br/> <br/>Good work, just keep shooting!</td>', 'Background not doing you any favours, but otherwise a compelling subject very good composition.  Crop a little tight on the bottom but otherwise he would''ve run out of head space!   Don''t be afraid to play with the camera settings.  If you do as I did, and sometimes still do, shoot on Auto, take a look at what the camera chose and the result you got.  Now, you can go to Manual mode and basically replicate those settings for a baseline, then mess around a little with the aperture and shutter speeds, and see what happens. Good work, just keep shooting!', '2009-09-03 20:29:23.000000', NULL, 0),
